Package: recodeStudio
Title: Interactive String-Variable Recoding Studio (Shiny)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Amelia", "Miramonti", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "amelia.miramonti@gmail.com")
Description: A dataset-agnostic Shiny application for cleaning messy string
    variables. Load any CSV or Excel file, normalize whole columns, browse
    unique values alphabetically or as string-similarity clusters, spellcheck
    with Hunspell, build recode rules with optional sibling-column
    propagation, and export canonical rule files plus a runnable dplyr script,
    or a cleaned copy of the data bundled with its provenance and the rules
    applied. The app never modifies the source data file.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
